# A-03 lean lock (Knowledge carousels)

Applies to **all** Knowledge / A-03 carousel and static work (desktop · mobile · cloud).

## On-frame default (fail closed)

- **Headline** + **one recognition sub-headline** only
- Sub-headline **is the whole message** (≤ ~2–4 short lines) — not a teaser
- Teaching depth → **caption**
- `explanation` / `takeaway` / body / bullet ladders → **off** unless the brief explicitly says `--dense`

## Content selection (before compose)

Supplied copy is a **pool**, not a requirement to show every sentence.

1. Pick the strongest headline (≤6 words · magenta accent ≤3 words)
2. Pick **one** recognition/support line
3. Move explanation + takeaway to caption
4. When in doubt, **REMOVE** on-frame copy — never add lines to fill whitespace

## Spokenness

Sub-headlines must read aloud as complete natural phrasing (2026-08-13). If mental reconstruction is needed, rewrite.

## Compositor

`apps/siya-health/brand/scripts/compose_format_a_knowledge.py` — lean default. Pass `--dense` only when explicitly requested.

**Sub-headline flag:** Pass the recognition/support line as `--recognition` (that is the sub-headline). Do not put it in `--explanation` / `--takeaway` / `--body` on lean frames.

## Reject

Dense teaching cards by default · equal visual weight for every copy block · Canva-template stacking · freehand `GenerateImage` as the final branded frame
